# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, correct.
#
# Both Dockerfiles run `bun ci` and then `COPY . .`. Without this file that
# second copy overwrites the freshly installed Linux node_modules with whatever
# the host has - on a Windows or macOS machine, binaries that cannot run in the
# image. It also shipped a 200MB+ context, which every Railway build pays for.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Generated. The server Dockerfile regenerates the OpenAPI spec during the build.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never send secrets into a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.local.example

# History and tooling the image has no use for.
.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.devcontainer
.agents
.playwright-mcp

# Test output.
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
playwright/.cache

# Documentation and local notes.
docs
*.md
!README.md

.DS_Store
